  Share time  |  Expiration date   \\n---|---|---|---  \\n  \\n##  No entries found in this folder \\n\\nName  |  State  |  Share time  |  Expiration date   \\n---|---|---|---  \\n  \\n##  No entries found in this folder \\n\\nName  |  State  |  Share time  |  Expiration date   \\n---|---|---|---  \\n  \\n##  No files in here \\n\\n##  No entries found in this folder \\n\\nName  |  Size  |  Modified   \\n---|---|---  \\n  \\n##  No deleted files \\n\\nYou will be able to recover deleted files from here \\n\\n##  No entries found in this folder \\n\\nSelect all  Name  [ Restore  ]() |  Deleted  [ Delete  ]()  \\n---|---  \\n  \\n|   \\n---|---  \\n  \\nmonitoring_disclosure.md  * \\n\\n1 \\n\\nXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX \\n\\n  * Upload \\n  * Folder \\n  * Text file \\n  * Document \\n  * Spreadsheet \\n  * Presentation \\n\\n\\n\\n\\n\\n', url='http://the-agent-company.com:8092/index.php/apps/files?dir=//Documents&fileid=135#editor', trigger_by_action='browse_interactive', error=False, observation='browse', goal_image_urls=[], open_pages_urls=['http://the-agent-company.com:8092/index.php/apps/files?dir=//Documents&fileid=135#editor'], active_page_index=0, last_browser_action=\"# Rename the new text file to desired name in the New menu textbox\\nfocus('1346')\\nclear('1346')\\nfill('1346', 'monitoring_disclosure.md')\\npress('1346', 'Enter')\\nnoop(1500)\", last_browser_action_error='', focused_element_bid='1358'), BrowseInteractiveAction(browser_actions='# Paste the policy content into the editor and save\\nfocus(\\'1358\\')\\nclear(\\'1358\\')\\nfill(\\'1358\\', \"# Remote Work Monitoring Policy\\\\n\\\\n## Purpose\\\\nTo ensure fairness and accountability in remote and hybrid work while maintaining productivity, safeguarding company data, and meeting legal and regulatory obligations. Monitoring supports transparency and consistent standards across teams.\\\\n\\\\n## Scope\\\\nThis policy applies to all employees and contractors who access Company systems, networks, or data, whether working remotely, on-site, or in a hybrid arrangement, and whether using Company\u2011owned devices or approved personal devices to access Company resources.\\\\n\\\\n## Policy Statement\\\\n- Use of Company systems and networks constitutes acknowledgment that activity may be monitored as described in this policy and related procedures.\\\\n- Monitoring is a standard business practice for security, compliance, service quality, and work accountability. Monitoring will be conducted in a professional and proportionate manner, consistent with applicable law.\\\\n- The Company strives to be transparent about its monitoring practices and will provide employees with clear notice of material changes.\\\\n\\\\n## Monitoring Methods\\\\nThe Company may collect, review, and retain information from the following sources:\\\\n- Endpoint and operating system telemetry (e.g., security agent signals, system logs, EDR alerts) on Company\u2011managed devices and approved BYOD devices enrolled in management.\\\\n- Network and remote access logs (e.g., VPN, SSO, firewall, and proxy/DNS logs).\\\\n- Application and collaboration platforms (e.g., email metadata, calendar metadata, messaging/collaboration tools, meeting platforms) for business records, usage, and security purposes.\\\\n- File and data protection systems (e.g., DLP, file access logs, cloud storage activity, versioning/audit events).\\\\n- Web filtering for security and acceptable use on Company\u2011managed devices and networks.\\\\n- Time, attendance, and activity logging where applicable to support payroll accuracy, resource planning, and fairness across teams.\\\\n\\\\nUnless separately noticed and legally permitted, the Company does not use keystroke logging or covert audio/video recording tools.\\\\n\\\\n## Employee Notice and Consent\\\\n- Employees will receive notice of active monitoring technologies through this policy, onboarding materials, and internal documentation listing currently deployed tools.\\\\n- Acknowledgment of the Employee Handbook and information security policies constitutes consent to the monitoring described herein, where consent is required by applicable law.\\\\n- The Company will provide advance notice of material changes to monitoring practices when feasible (target 14 days), subject to urgent security or legal requirements.\\\\n\\\\n## Use of Monitoring Data\\\\nMonitoring data may be used for:\\\\n- Security and incident response, including threat detection, investigation, and remediation.\\\\n- Compliance with legal, regulatory, audit, and contractual requirements.\\\\n- Performance management and workload planning where appropriate and lawful.\\\\n- Investigations of suspected misconduct, policy violations, or unlawful activity.\\\\n- Service reliability, capacity planning, and quality assurance.\\\\n\\\\nMonitoring data will not be used to track non\u2011work activity or personal time and will not be used in a manner that unlawfully discriminates or violates labor protections.\\\\n\\\\n## Privacy Safeguards\\\\n- Personal accounts and personal communications on non\u2011Company services are not monitored, except to the extent they traverse Company networks or systems and are captured in routine security logs.\\\\n- Off\u2011hours activity is not monitored for non\u2011exempt employees except for basic security events (e.g., login attempts) or where required by law, policy, or incident response.\\\\n- Audio, video, or screen recording will only occur with notice and for defined business purposes, except where otherwise permitted by law in the context of investigations.\\\\n- Geolocation data collection is limited to what is necessary for security, compliance, or asset protection and only on Company\u2011managed or enrolled devices.\\\\n\\\\n## BYOD and Company\u2011Managed Devices\\\\n- Access to Company data from personal devices may require mobile device management (MDM) enrollment or the use of a secure container/application. The Company may enforce security controls (e.g., passcode, encryption) and may remove corporate data from personal devices upon policy violation or separation.\\\\n- The Company does not access the personal content of BYOD devices; actions are limited to managing or removing Company data and enforcing security settings.\\\\n\\\\n## Data Retention and Access Controls\\\\n- Monitoring data will be retained consistent with the Company\u2019s Records Retention Schedule and legal hold obligations.\\\\n- Access to monitoring data is restricted to authorized personnel (e.g., Security, IT, HR, Legal, and management with a need to know) and is subject to confidentiality and auditing requirements.\\\\n\\\\n## Jurisdiction and Compliance\\\\n- Monitoring activities will comply with applicable laws, including but not limited to U.S. state privacy and wiretap/consent laws, CPRA, and GDPR where applicable. Where required, jurisdiction\u2011specific notices or consents will be obtained.\\\\n- In the event of a conflict between this policy and local law, local law controls.\\\\n\\\\n## Employee Responsibilities\\\\n- Use Company systems and data responsibly and in accordance with Company policies.\\\\n- Do not attempt to disable, evade, or tamper with monitoring or security controls.\\\\n\\\\n## Questions and Appeals\\\\nEmployees with questions or concerns, or who wish to challenge the accuracy of monitoring data, should contact HR or the Information Security team. The Company will review and address inquiries in a timely manner.\\\\n\\\\n## Violations and Discipline\\\\nViolations of this policy or attempts to circumvent monitoring or security controls may result in corrective action, up to and including termination, subject to local laws and applicable collective agreements.\\\\n\\\\n## Transparency Commitment\\\\nThe Company will maintain an internal page listing the primary monitoring and security tools in use and will notify employees before material changes when feasible. Monitoring is a condition of using Company systems and accessing Company data.\")\\npress(\\'1358\\', \\'ControlOrMeta+s\\')\\nnoop(1200)\\n# Return to Documents listing to share the file\\nclick(\\'334\\')\\nnoop(1500)\\n# Filter by file name to find it quickly\\nfocus(\\'224\\')\\nfill(\\'224\\', \\'monitoring_disclosure.md\\')\\npress(\\'224\\', \\'Enter\\')\\nnoop(1500)', thought='', browsergym_send_msg_to_user='', action='browse_interactive', security_risk=None), BrowserOutputObservation(content='This application requires JavaScript for correct operation. Please [ enable JavaScript ](http://enable-javascript.com/) and reload the page. \\n\\n[ ownCloud 10.1.1 is available. Get more information on how to update. ](https://doc.owncloud.com/server/latest/admin_manual/maintenance/upgrading/upgrade.html)\\n\\n[ There were problems with the code integrity check. More information\u2026 ](/index.php/settings/admin#security-warning)\\n\\n# [ ownCloud  ](/index.php) <::before> Menu  Files \\n\\n<::after>\\n\\ntheagentcompany \\n\\n  * [ Settings ](/index.php/settings/personal)\\n  * [ Users ](/index.php/settings/users)\\n  * [ Help ](/index.php/settings/help)\\n  * [ Log out ](http://the-agent-company.com:8092/index.php/logout?requesttoken=SjEtAGZNFFFkFR9%2BGB0/NyMFW14iARsaPgJXDkcVVn0%3D%3AscgwPfNg4LwJOpydTq2oxtxNWKgkuV30xPWuhi8pe1Y%3D)\\n\\n\\n\\n##  No notifications \\n\\nSearch \\n\\n  * [ Files  ](/index.php/apps/files/)\\n  * [ Gallery  ](/index.php/apps/gallery/)\\n  * [ Office  ](/index.php/apps/richdocuments/index)\\n  * [ Text  ](/index.php/apps/files_textviewer/)\\n  * [ Music  ](/index.php/apps/music/)\\n  * [ Market  ](/index.php/apps/market/)\\n\\n\\n\\n  * All files \\n  * Favorites \\n  * Shared with you \\n  * Shared with others \\n  * Shared by link \\n  * Tags \\n  * Deleted files \\n\\n\\n\\nSettings \\n\\nShow hidden files \\n\\nWebDAV  _Use this address to[ access your Files via WebDAV ](https://doc.owncloud.org/server/10.0/go.p